    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (76.097) and **Trea Turner** (75.398). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier offensive engine, boasting an elite 0.479 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Englert, making him our highest-scoring play despite a slight park penalty. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.576) benefit significantly from a soft matchup against Avila (5.01 xERA). **Trea Turner** remains the cornerstone for our stolen base strategy, and while we keep an eye on the opposing pitcher's 50% hold rate, the combination of his leadoff position and the pitcher's poor expected ERA cements his status as an essential start. **Junior Caminero** (73.072) also warrants mention as a top-tier option, maintaining strong efficiency despite a neutral matchup against Lambert.\n\nThe decision to start **Casey Schmitt** (62.255) over **Luke Raley** (58.134) was the most difficult call of the day. **Casey Schmitt** earned the nod primarily due to a 14% park-factor boost and a dynamic platoon advantage against Gordon, which tipped the scale in his favor despite **Luke Raley**'s solid profile. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Caleb Durbin** (64.897); though we have slotted him into the five-hole based on projected order, any shift toward the bottom of the lineup could dampen his scoring potential. We continue to prioritize stolen base threats like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.472), whose 10% leadoff bonus and favorable matchup against the lefty Liberatore help offset his dynamic platoon disadvantage. While **Dillon Dingler** (47.578) remains in the lineup, his low score reflects a challenging dynamic platoon penalty; he remains a volume play for our catching slot, but he is the softest component of today\u2019s starting nine.",
